bile-orders","isClickable":false},{"name":"Quick Service","urlFriendlyId":"quick-service","url":"/dining/#/quick-service","isClickable":false}]}],"accessibilityModal":{"data":[{"title":"Accessibility","data":[{"size":"m","text":"Guest May Remain in Wheelchair/ECV"}],"variant":"icon"},{"title":"Guest Policies","data":{"bulleted":[{"text":"<p><span>Alcoholic beverages may be purchased at the Disneyland Resort by Guests 21 years of age or older. The documents required to verify age vary for United States residents and non-United States residents.</span></p><p><strong><br />United States Residents</strong></p><p>United States residents who wish to purchase an alcoholic beverage at the Disneyland Resort must present one of the following forms of identification:</p><p>•        Identification card issued by a governmental agency in the United States (Federal, State, Territory,* County, City) that contains the following:</p><p>o   Name</p><p>o   Date of birth</p><p>o   Physical description of the person</p><p>o   Photo of the person</p><p>o   Expiration date</p><p>•        Valid active United States Armed Forces ID (must include date of birth and portrait photo)</p><p>•        Valid original passport</p><p>Temporary driver’s licenses, temporary ID cards and copies of passports, driver’s licenses or ID cards are not acceptable.</p><p>* United States territories include Puerto Rico, Guam, Northern Mariana Islands, United States Virgin Islands and American Samoa.</p><p><strong><br />Non-United States Residents</strong></p><p>Original passports are the only form of identification acceptable for Guests from outside the United States; non-United States driver’s licenses, ID cards, temporary ID cards and copies of ID cards are not acceptable.</p>"}],"icon":[]},"variant":"combined"}],"title":"Safety, Accessibility and Guest Policies","ctaTitle":"Show  Safety, Accessibility and Guest Policies","ariaLabel":"Open Modal for Safety, Accessibility and Guest Policies","titleAttribute":"Op